   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law, in relation to making a technical correction relating to the process of selling surplus fire equipment and vehicles",
    "basePrintNo": "S5995",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5995-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §176, Town L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5995\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the town law, in relation to making\na technical correction relating to the process of selling surplus fire\nequipment and vehicles\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe bill amends an incorrect reference in a section of the Town Law to\na subdivision of the General Municipal Law, which was renumbered by\nChapter 234 of the Laws of 2006.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would correct a reference in Town Law section 176(23) to\nsubdivision 4 of section six-g of the General Municipal Law that was\nrenumbered to subdivision 7 in Chapter 234 of the Laws of 2006.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nThe law would remain in full force and effect with this statutory\nchange.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis legislation will correct a statutory reference in Section 176\n(23) of the Town Law to subdivision 4 of Section 6(g) of the General\nMunicipal Law.\n\nThe correction subdivision reference should be to subdivision 7 of\nsection six-g of General Municipal Law, as renumbered in Chapter 234\nof the Laws of 2006.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
